# Display modes. Included before ./exec so no client maps against a mode that is about to
# change under it.
#
# The G24-20 is a 165 Hz panel and advertises 1920x1080 at 50/60/100/120/144/165 Hz, but
# wlroots settles on 60 and sway reported `1920x1080@60.0` for it on this host
# [2026-08-28, `swaymsg -t get_outputs`]. 60 Hz is not merely fewer frames, it is no
# headroom: a 60 fps game vsynced to a 60 Hz scanout drops a whole frame for every hitch,
# which is what "it is dropping frames" looks like from the chair.
#
# Identified by make/model/serial rather than by connector name, because the connector is
# not stable for this monitor. Plugged into the motherboard it is DP-4 on the Intel iGPU
# (pci-0000:00:02.0); plugged into the RTX 3060 it becomes one of that card's own
# DP-1/DP-2/DP-3 (pci-0000:01:00.0). The identifier string survives the move, a connector
# name silently stops matching.
#
# The refresh value is sway's own, to the digit it reports. `165Hz` is not what the mode
# list contains and sway matches modes, it does not round to them.
#
# 165 Hz is verified on the iGPU port, not hoped for: this exact line loaded and applied on
# a fresh sway start, and the identifier was separately confirmed to match the live output
# [2026-08-28, both in packages/sway/README.md §Never run `sway` to check a config — the
# first of those two was an accident, and that section exists so it is not repeated]. The
# 60 Hz was purely mode selection; nothing about the link or the iGPU requires it.
output "Lenovo Group Limited G24-20 U533A88N" mode 1920x1080@164.997Hz

# Not enabled here: `adaptive_sync on`. The panel supports it and VRR is the real answer to
# an occasional missed frame — the scanout waits for the frame instead of showing the
# previous one twice. It is left off because sway only engages VRR when one surface is
# driving the output, and this desktop always has mpvpaper drawing a looping video
# wallpaper behind everything, so the win is conditional while the flicker risk on a
# budget panel is not. Turn it on deliberately, watch for brightness pumping on dark
# scenes, not as part of a mode change.
